        "body": "Stage 2a, Task 15 (plan `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-26-df-installer-stage2a.md`): live stand acceptance — code and docs. Per ruling R15-3 this PR ships the workflow and an evidence **skeleton**; the live run is dispatched by the owner on `master` after merge (environment `df-stage2-live`: required reviewer, master only), and a follow-up PR (15e) fills evidence from that run and closes TODO.\n\n- `.github/workflows/df-stage2-live.yml` — `workflow_dispatch` only, environment `df-stage2-live`, `if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/master'`, matrix macos-15 / ubuntu-24.04, pinned actions, `persist-credentials: false`; three phases `install` → `stand` → `wipe`; secrets reach only the steps after provenance; secret files 0600 in `RUNNER_TEMP`, removed in `always()`.\n- Provenance before any secret: blob pairs of `FIXTURE_FROM_CHECKOUT` equal between checkout@`github.sha` and fixture@`fixture_sha`; `release.json` names `fixture_sha`; `admin_digest` == new `df.admin.expected_admin_digest(<checkout>/df)`.\n- `tests/df/live_stand.py` — rows 1–9 of §4.5 against the private stand, each with its refusal mechanism and feasibility control; explicit row dependencies (a skipped row is never a pass); overall fail if any row fails; tokens revoked at the end.\n- `tests/df/gate_proxy.py` — 127.0.0.1 proxy to api.github.com holding the first review POST (row 4б, read→publish window through the real publisher).\n- Row 5 control without a ruleset (R15-1/R15-1a): a PR deliberately conflicting with a temporary branch; `mergeable == false` asserted before the full-installation-token PUT → 405.\n- Machine token: classic PAT of a stand-only machine user (R15-2); evidence records the type only.\n- README stage-2a section, CLAUDE.md `df/` line, TODO note; `sudo_refused` moved to `tests/df/roles_world.py`.\n\nOffline: `tests/df/test_live_stand.py` (provenance incl. `test_live_provenance`, row dependency logic, push-refusal matcher, ps-window check). Nothing in pytest reads `DF_STAND_*` or touches the network.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
        "closed_at": "2026-10-30T10:53:13Z",
